# iCloud Drive conflict copies. This repository lives in iCloud Drive, which
# resolves a sync conflict by writing "<name> 2.<ext>" beside the original
# instead of merging. Sixteen accumulated here unnoticed, one of them a second
# copy of a scheduled workflow — committing that would have registered the
# collector's cron twice. Two more landed inside .git/ itself, where a stray
# refs/heads/main 2 pointing at an August commit made git read it as a branch
# whose name contains a space and fail every fetch with "bad object
# refs/heads/main 2". No tracked file here has a space in its name, so this
# pattern cannot hide real work.
* [2-9].*
